# Line endings, repository-wide.
#
# This repository is developed on Windows and run on Linux, so `core.autocrlf` is on for
# somebody and off for somebody else, and the difference is not cosmetic:
#
#   * a CRLF in a shell script turns `#!/bin/bash` into `#!/bin/bash\r`, and the shell
#     reports `bad interpreter: No such file or directory` or `$'\r': command not found`
#     -- an hour of confusion for a byte nobody typed;
#   * a CRLF in `chtc/requirements.txt` glues a carriage return onto the
#     `--extra-index-url` line and the cu121 torch wheels stop resolving;
#   * a CRLF in an HTCondor submit file is passed through into the job's environment.
#
# `chtc/.gitattributes` has said this for the cluster layer since the first job failed on
# it. This file says it for the whole tree, because `scripts/get_data.sh` and
# `experiments/scoring/rebuild.sh` are outside that directory and are the two scripts a
# stranger runs first.
#
# `eol=lf` is checked out as LF whatever the cloner's `core.autocrlf` says.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.sub   text eol=lf
*.dag   text eol=lf
*.def   text eol=lf
*.conf  text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.cff   text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.info  text eol=lf
*.example text eol=lf
LICENSE text eol=lf

# Binary: never touched, never diffed as text.
*.npy   binary
*.npz   binary
*.pt    binary
*.h5    binary
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.zarr  binary
